 "coverage_guards": [
  {
   "query": "queries.scm",
   "capabilities": [
    "definitions"
   ],
   "reason": "A key is stated where it is written, and nothing more is claimed about it. JSON5 carries no schema of its own, so the Pack cannot tell a dependency table from an ordinary object, a property name from a value, or a version range from a file path; what a key means is the knowledge of the tool that reads the file."
  },
  {
   "query": "queries.scm",
   "capabilities": [
    "definitions"
   ],
   "reason": "A value is carried with its key only when it is a string, a number, a boolean or null. A key set to an object or an array is stated without a value, because the keys and strings inside it are their own emissions; asking what such a key is set to returns its members, not its text."
  },
  {
   "query": "queries.scm",
   "capabilities": [
    "definitions"
   ],
   "reason": "A string is stored as it is written, with only its surrounding quotes removed. This grammar makes a string a single leaf token, so escapes are not visible to a pattern and are not decoded: a key or value spelled \"C:\\tools\" or \"aAb\" is stored in that escaped spelling, and a line continuation inside a multi-line string keeps its backslash and newline. Such a name matches a declaration elsewhere only if that one is spelled the same way."
  },
  {
   "query": "queries.scm",
   "capabilities": [
    "references"
   ],
   "reason": "A string listed in an array is stated under its own text and nothing else. JSON5 has no syntax that says what such a string refers to, so a link to a declaration elsewhere is by name alone: a package name, a file path, a glob and an enum member are indistinguishable, and a match is not proof of a dependency."
  },
  {
   "query": "queries.scm",
   "capabilities": [
    "definitions"
   ],
   "reason": "A comment is not stated. JSON5 allows `//` and `/* */` where JSON does not, but a comment resolves against nothing and naming one by its own prose would add a row per line of commentary in every file; the reason a key is set to a value is not recoverable from the file."
  }
 ],
